Another really good one on this&nbsp;
list... Tom, did you see Coco?

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:02.560
I never saw Coco.

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:03.510
That is a Pixar movie so...

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:09.120
Coco is a good one, where he connects&nbsp;
with his grandma and plays the song&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:17.040
that her father had played for her. And again,&nbsp;
my wife and I saw that in the theaters and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:22.080
we just were weeping. But that was a weirdly&nbsp;
emotional day for us for some reason, because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:26.960
that was the movie that opened with the Olaf's&nbsp;
insane Christmas short, the 20 minute short?

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:28.372
The one that had to be removed, yeah.

00:13:28.372 --> 00:13:29.440
That's why it was emotional?

00:13:29.440 --> 00:13:31.840
That made us cry too and I don't know why.

00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:34.160
Oh, okay. I thought you were saying&nbsp;
that you were just particularly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:37.680
vulnerable that day because you&nbsp;
got to watch so much extra Olaf.

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:43.120
I don't know what it was, but Olaf going around&nbsp;
trying to find what makes everybody happy on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:49.200
the holidays smashed my soul. It was just like,&nbsp;
"You're going to cry now because holidays&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:52.080
are magic." And I was just like, "Yeah, they&nbsp;
are magic." "Everybody has a special holiday."

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:53.840
It's like taking whatever drug they give you when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:55.040
you get your wisdom teeth taken&nbsp;
out, you're just like, "Aah."

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:57.920
Brian, have you ever cried over&nbsp;
Nutcracker and the Four Realms?

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:01.280
I need to see that movie, I need to watch it.

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:02.240
Maybe it'll make you cry.

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:03.440
I hope so.

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:04.580
I'd like-

00:14:04.960 --> 00:14:08.240
I feel like Tom cried at Taxi Driver&nbsp;
or something once, something really-

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:13.520
"He just wanted to drive his taxi."

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:15.840
"I think that mohawk looks really good."

00:14:16.640 --> 00:14:19.360
Man, the version of me that&nbsp;
lives in your heads is-

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:25.680
"I am talking to you. I am talking to&nbsp;
you. I'm trying to be your friend."

00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:26.160
"You're not alone."

00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:27.360
"I just want to communicate."

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:30.080
"We're trying to have a dialogue."

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:32.640
"You did a really good job&nbsp;
making a slidey gun." Yeah.

00:14:34.480 --> 00:14:36.960
The only other one I want to&nbsp;
add that isn't on this list,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:37.760 --> 00:14:42.800
but for me... You mentioned that apparently&nbsp;
you're more susceptible to crying on planes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:47.663
which is really good to know because I saw&nbsp;
Moana on a plane and that got me immediately.

00:14:47.663 --> 00:14:50.400
It did?
So did I, yeah.

00:14:50.400 --> 00:14:56.720
Oh my God. And I have PTSD from it because&nbsp;
we play the soundtrack for our kid sometimes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:56.720 --> 00:15:03.600
and even that fun opening song when they&nbsp;
sing that line, "And no one leaves," and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:08.080
I'm just like, "Oh, no one leaves. Because&nbsp;
they used to be wayfarers, they used to-"

00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:11.840
I cried at the end of that movie, and I&nbsp;
was flying with my friend who's like...&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.623 --> 00:15:19.920
if a Shiba Inu was a person, she doesn't cry&nbsp;
a lot. And I was like, "Oh no, I don't want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:24.080
her to see me cry. I've never cried in front&nbsp;
of her, this is so weird." But I looked over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:28.640
and she was crying too, and I was like, "Yes,&nbsp;
thank God. Okay, we're both losers, it's fine."

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:33.600
Yeah. I told my wife on the flight, I watched&nbsp;
that on the flight and she fell asleep and I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:37.120
was just like, "You should watch Moana. It made&nbsp;
me cry a lot." And she watched and she was like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:41.840
"That was fine." No reaction to it. She&nbsp;
was like, "Yeah, I guess it was okay."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:45.520
The only other instance I can think of&nbsp;
where that kind of thing happened on a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:45.520 --> 00:15:50.080
plane was I saw Game Night on a plane. I&nbsp;
didn't cry, I just laughed like an idiot.

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:52.080
You didn't cry during Game Night?

00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:54.720
No, I didn't cry during Game Night, but&nbsp;
I was worried that people were going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:57.040
want to change seats because&nbsp;
I was laughing like a maniac.

00:15:57.840 --> 00:15:59.280
Try crying next time, they will move.

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:02.680
I'd get my own seat, finally.

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:07.375
That should get a lot of&nbsp;
people shot by an air marshal.

00:16:08.935 --> 00:16:12.240
Thanks for watching, please hit like&nbsp;
and subscribe. And if you watch this far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:15.920
please hit something and leave a&nbsp;
